 "brief": "1) YESTERDAY AT A GLANCE\nNet sales: 5325 AED, orders: 96, average order: 55 AED. Down 29.3% vs same weekday last week. Hours that underperformed vs their 4-week baseline: 10:00 (-40%), 15:00 (-53.8%), 16:00 (-84.2%).\n\n2) WHAT THE NUMBERS SAY\n- Dead hours: 16:00 (2.9 avg orders) and 15:00 (3.4 avg orders) are the weakest, with 16:00 yesterday down 84.2% vs baseline.\n- Weakest days: Saturday (102.8 avg orders, -6.4% vs week avg) and Wednesday (99.5 avg orders, -5.9% vs week avg).\n- Weak items: Beef Burrito Bowl (408 units, -17% trend) and Tuna Power Salad (197 units, 3.1% trend but low share).\n- Promo economics: Promo orders have a 51 AED average order vs 64 AED for non-promo orders, with 12398 AED discount cost in 28 days.\n\n3) MARKET WATCH\nNo relevant competitor news this month. Market trends include telehealth-linked nutrition products, cloud kitchen growth, meal kit delivery services, and meal replacement products.\n\n4) OFFERS TO RUN\nEarly Bird Bundle | Why: 16:00 dead hour (2.9 avg orders, yesterday -84.2% vs baseline) | Mechanic: Buy any Bowl, get free Energy Balls (min spend 50 AED) | When: Mon-Fri 15:00-17:00 | Channel: Direct | Goal: Increase orders in 15:00-17:00 by 20%\nBurrito Boost | Why: Beef Burrito Bowl declining (-17% trend) | Mechanic: Buy Beef Burrito Bowl, get 20% off Protein Brownie | When: All days, all hours | Channel: Talabat | Goal: Increase Beef Burrito Bowl sales by 15%\nWeekend Kickoff | Why: Saturday is weakest day (-6.4% vs week avg) | Mechanic: Spend 100 AED, get 20% off entire order | When: Saturday 12:00-14:00 and 19:00-21:00 | Channel: Deliveroo | Goal: Increase Saturday orders by 10%\n\n5) WATCH TOMORROW\nCheck if 15:00-17:00 orders increase with the Early Bird Bundle.\nMonitor Beef Burrito Bowl sales with the Burrito Boost offer.\n\nDemo data"
